The failing job is caused by the wrong substrate linker setup for the roothide/Theos fork, not by the packaging step itself.
What the workflow and source say:
• In .github/workflows/build.yml, the job explicitly documents the issue:
• $THEOS/include is empty
• $THEOS/lib has no substrate
• the real substrate lives in theos/vendor/include and theos/vendor/lib/CydiaSubstrate.framework
• The build step is Build Package, and the failure is -lsubstrate/substrate link resolution.
• scripts/build.sh also contains the fix: it checks for theos/vendor/lib/CydiaSubstrate.framework and switches to -Ftheos/vendor/lib -framework CydiaSubstrate.
The fix is to link against the roothide vendor layout instead of the default Theos layout.
